<p>An Australian court has granted bail to former SAS soldier Ben Roberts-Smith, a Victoria Cross recipient, after he spent about 10 days in custody following his arrest on five war-crime murder charges linked to Afghanistan. Prosecutors say that between 2009 and 2012, he murdered or helped procure the murders of five unarmed Afghan civilians in Uruzgan province. Each charge carries a maximum sentence of life imprisonment. The ruling means Roberts-Smith will be released under strict conditions, including travel restrictions, while prosecutors continue building a case that could go to trial. The case is one of Australia’s highest-profile war-crimes matters and comes after years of public scrutiny, beginning with media reports in 2018 and later a civil defamation ruling that found substantial truth in allegations that he was involved in unlawful killings in Afghanistan.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/D71zgPGZqwMp1X3rI3s5rnH09hyh53lTPfdvRWNhSMYqELBleOG7u4wFVEsOxN3R5448sVAOC66wgB27tb3p53rDDTXIA7G2uz3x9tZEaUI5ByF4VIjCoPrerqn19OMdQUU8csYLp-whfZVU5e140hYKcXETbXadFiaoGhtMEA' alt='Ben Roberts-Smith, the former Australian soldier charged with war crimes, in a file image.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Geographic spread: The five counts are tied to operations at Kakarak, Darwan and Syahchow in Uruzgan province, suggesting prosecutors are alleging wrongdoing across multiple raids rather than a single episode.</li><li>Inquiry scope: Japan Today said the prosecution follows a sweeping war-crimes investigation into Australian military conduct in Afghanistan, underscoring that this case is part of a broader effort.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Court documents: One allegation cited by Michael West says Roberts-Smith ordered a soldier identified only as Person 4 to kill Mohammed Essa during the April 2009 Kakarak raid. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/accused-war-criminal-ben-roberts-smith-to-seek-freedom/'>Michael West</a>)</li><li>Official records: Michael West reported that two of the dead men were originally recorded as enemies killed in action, highlighting a gap between contemporaneous military records and the prosecution case. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/accused-war-criminal-ben-roberts-smith-to-seek-freedom/'>Michael West</a>)</li><li>Public image: The Guardian described Roberts-Smith as once Australia’s most lionised soldier, highlighting how sharply the charges clash with his earlier national reputation. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/apr/17/ben-roberts-smith-brs-bail-decision-war-crimes-trial-ntwnfb'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/accused-war-criminal-ben-roberts-smith-to-seek-freedom/'>Accused war criminal Ben Roberts-Smith to seek freedom</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/australias-decorated-veteran-granted-bail-war-crimes-charges-132127516'>Australia&#x27;s most decorated veteran granted bail on war crimes charges related to Afghan deaths</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/17/australian-ex-soldier-roberts-smith-granted-bail-in-afghan-war-crimes-case'>Australian ex-soldier Roberts-Smith granted bail in Afghan war crimes case</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/apr/17/ben-roberts-smith-brs-bail-decision-war-crimes-trial-ntwnfb'>Ben Roberts-Smith granted bail after being charged with five counts of war crime murder</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/australian-soldier-accused-of-war-crimes-in-afghanistan-granted-bail'>Australian soldier accused of war crimes in Afghanistan granted bail</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/australian-former-soldier-gets-bail-afghanistan-war-crime-charges'>Australian former soldier gets bail on Afghanistan war crime charges</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href